  "body": "# Notion: Notion Skills API (2026-09-17, 23.79s, 1920x1080)\nType: feature launch\nLink: https://x.com/NotionHQ/status/2100619682718118397\n\n## One-line style\nWarm off-white canvas, word-by-word headlines, real app windows that fade in, push and stack.\n\n## Structure\n| Time | Beat | On screen | Motion |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0-1.9 | hook | Warm off-white bg, centred two-line headline \"Edit skills together / in Notion\" | Words appear one at a time in their final positions, ~0.1s apart; hold ~1.2s |\n| 1.9-3.3 | reveal | Real Notion page in a macOS browser window (traffic lights, tabs), window ~90% frame width with soft shadow | Text cuts away; window fades in from 0 to 1 opacity over ~0.6s while rising slightly; then camera pushes in to ~1.6x on the page body (~0.5s, power2.inOut) |\n| 3.3-5.3 | demo | Close crop of page: page icon, grey placeholder title \"New skill\", property rows | Title types in (\"Compile quarterly report\"), ~3 chars/frame |\n| 5.3-7.3 | transition | Headline card \"Sync them to GitHub\" (one line) | Words appear one at a time, hold ~1.3s |\n| 7.3-8.6 | demo | Notion window again at a medium crop | Slow drift / push-in (~3% over 1.3s) |\n| 8.6-10.6 | proof | GitHub repo file list in a browser window, ~65% frame width, centred | Cross-fade from Notion (~0.4s) with window settling from slightly larger to final size; at ~10.0s a new row slides in at the top of the list, pushing the rows down (~0.3s, power2.out) |\n| 10.6-12.3 | proof | Same GitHub list, crop ~1.6x | Fast camera push-in ~0.3s (power3.inOut), then hold |\n| 12.3-14.77 | transition | Headline \"Use skills with any agent\" | Word-by-word, hold ~1.7s |\n| 14.77-15.7 | demo | Desktop chat app window (grey sidebar, white modal showing the skill), ~95% frame width | Hard cut (measured 14.77) |\n| 15.7-17.3 | demo | Web chat app window with the skill page arrives in front; the previous window recedes behind it | Old window scales ~1.0 to ~0.65 and moves up (~0.6s, power2.out) while the new window cross-fades in at full size (~0.5s) |\n| 17.3-18.6 | demo | Third window (another chat app's plugin page) stacks in front; two receded windows peek above it | Same stack shuffle (~0.6s) |\n| 18.6-20.6 | lockup | Headline \"One home for every skill\" | Word-by-word, hold ~1.5s |\n| 20.6-23.6 | lockup | Notion cube logo alone (~6% height), then logo + \"Notion\" wordmark centred | Hard cut to logo; wordmark appears to the right at ~21.6s; hold ~2s |\n| 23.6-23.79 | lockup | Black | Hard cut |\n\n## Pacing\nMeasured: 1 hard cut detected (14.77s), avg shot 11.89s, median 14.77s. Visually it is built from ~10 beats of ~1.3-2.5s each. Detection misses them because the transitions are fades, pushes and window stacks on a near-white background. The camera move inside each beat carries the continuity. Text cards hold ~1.2-1.7s after the last word lands. The pace stays steady throughout, with no acceleration at the end. The lockup holds ~3s. Cuts on beat: 0/1.\n\n## Typography\n- Neutral grotesk sans (Inter-like), semibold ~600, normal width, slightly tight tracking. Near-black #151515.\n- Size ~9% of frame height, on one line or two balanced lines.\n- Sentence case, no ending punctuation.\n- 4-5 words per card.\n- Entry: words appear one at a time in their pre-laid final positions (no slide, near-instant opacity), ~0.08-0.12s apart. The block is centred from the start, so nothing shifts as words arrive. Exit: hard cut or straight swap to the next shot.\n- In-UI typing at native UI size (page title ~5% height when cropped).\n- Alignment: centred.\n\n## Color and texture\n- Background warm off-white #F6F5F1 everywhere, including the lockup. Final frame black.\n- UI is real, so it carries its own colors: white windows #FFFFFF, Notion blue banner #E8F1FB with link blue #2F7FD8, GitHub folder blue #54AEFF, a few red/green property chips.\n- Text #151515.\n- Windows have a large soft shadow (~0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.10)).\n- No grain, gradients or glow. The look is quiet and paper-like.\n\n## Product UI treatment\nReal screenshots/recordings of actual apps (Notion, GitHub, desktop and web chat apps) in macOS browser/app windows with traffic lights and tab bars. Framing goes from a full window to a cropped detail through smooth camera pushes. There is no cursor. Typing appears only in the Notion title. Multi-app interoperability is shown as a stack of windows, with older ones receding up and back like a card deck. UI detail is high, but the crops pick one area of interest.\n\n## Motion vocabulary\n- Word-by-word headline: each word opacity 0 to 1 in ~1 frame, stagger ~0.1s, ease none.\n- Window fade-in: opacity 0 to 1 over ~0.6s with y +2% to 0, power2.out.\n- Camera push into UI: scale 1 to ~1.6, ~0.3-0.5s, power3.inOut, anchored on the area of interest. Slow drift pushes of ~3% over 1-2s, ease none.\n- Cross-fade between apps: ~0.4s, with the incoming window settling from scale ~1.05 to 1.\n- List row insert: existing rows translate down by one row height (~0.3s, power2.out); new row fades in.\n- Window stack shuffle: the front window goes to scale ~0.65 and y -30% (moves up and back) over ~0.6s with power2.out. The new window fades in at front, full size, ~0.5s. Earlier windows peek above the top edge.\n- Lockup: hard cut to the logo, then the wordmark appears ~1s later with no visible motion.\n- Transitions: text cards are hard cuts. UI-to-UI changes are fades and pushes.\n\n## Sound (measured only)\nAudio present. Tempo estimate ~109 BPM. Cuts on beat: 0/1. No visual hits such as flashes or shakes. Unclear beyond that.\n\n## Signature techniques\n1. **In-place word reveal**: render the whole centred headline with each word in a span at opacity 0, then `tl.to(words,{opacity:1,duration:0.03,stagger:0.1,ease:\"none\"})`. Inter 600, ~9vh, on #F6F5F1. Hold 1.5s, then hard cut.\n2. **Window fade-up then push**: put a macOS-chrome browser frame (screenshot inside) at 90% width with a soft shadow. `from({opacity:0,yPercent:2,duration:0.6,ease:\"power2.out\"})`, then `to(stage,{scale:1.6,transformOrigin:\"30% 40%\",duration:0.45,ease:\"power3.inOut\"})` to crop to the detail.\n3. **Window deck stack**: when the next app comes in, the current front window animates `{scale:0.65,yPercent:-32,duration:0.6,ease:\"power2.out\"}` and the new window fades in at scale 1 on top. Keep receded windows visible peeking above, each further one smaller.\n4. **Row insert proof**: in a table, tween existing rows `y:+rowH` (0.3s, power2.out) and fade in the new top row. Follow with a quick camera push onto it.\n5. **Quiet lockup**: on the same off-white, show the logo mark alone at ~6vh for ~1s, then the wordmark beside it. Hold ~2s, then cut to black.\n\n## Rules to copy\n- Keep one warm off-white background for the whole film, text cards and UI alike.\n- Alternate one-line or two-line word-by-word headlines with real product windows.\n- Never animate the text position: words pop in place, then hard cut.\n- Show real UI in real window chrome with a soft shadow. No mock simplification.\n- Move between full window and detail with smooth, quick camera pushes, not cuts.\n- Show \"works everywhere\" by stacking app windows like a deck, each new one in front.\n- Keep beats at ~1.5-2.5s and end with a ~3s logo + wordmark hold."
