  "description": "Notion: Button automations that message agents (2026-10-15, 17.13s, 1920x1080). Silent, text-free screen recording with snappy motion-blurred zooms that follow the cursor.",
  "body": "# Notion: Button automations that message agents (2026-10-15, 17.13s, 1920x1080)\nType: feature launch\nLink: https://x.com/NotionHQ/status/2110853125389029437\n\n## One-line style\nSilent, text-free screen recording with snappy motion-blurred zooms that follow the cursor.\n\n## Structure\n| Time | Beat | On screen | Motion |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0-0.33 | hook | Whole Notion window (database \"Feature requests\") floating on a light warm-grey field with soft shadow, ~78% frame width | Static, cursor already on the \"Button\" column header |\n| 0.33-0.6 | transition | Same, zooming in to the column header area | Fast zoom ~0.85x to ~2x scale over ~0.3s with heavy motion blur (power3.inOut) |\n| 0.6-1.67 | demo | Cropped table, property menu open; cursor clicks \"Edit automation\" | Hold, small cursor moves |\n| 1.67-2.9 | demo | Hard cut (measured 1.67): automation modal over a grey-dimmed table (\"When: Button is clicked\", \"Do: New action\") | Cursor moves to \"New action\" and clicks |\n| 2.9-3.35 | transition | Action search menu opens | Camera pans down ~25% of frame and recentres with motion blur (~0.35s, power2.inOut) |\n| 3.35-5.0 | demo | Long action menu; cursor slides down to \"Send message to agent\" | Row hover highlight follows the cursor |\n| 5.0-5.7 | demo | Menu closes, \"Send message to\" block with empty Message field appears | Menu fades out (~0.15s); new block appears in place |\n| 5.7-6.1 | transition | | Camera re-frames up/in on the Message field with blur (~0.35s) |\n| 6.1-10.6 | demo | Typing \"Give me a TLDR on @this\", mention menu, picks \"This page\" chip; cursor clicks Save | Live typing at recording speed; a mention dropdown pops |\n| 10.6-11.3 | demo | Modal closes, back to the table with property menu | Modal disappears instantly |\n| 11.3-13.5 | demo | Hard cut (measured 11.3): table crop; cursor clicks a \"TLDR\" button cell | Slight drift |\n| 13.5-16.3 | proof | Page \"Add H5 headers to Notion\" opens with the AI side panel; the reply streams in as a paragraph | Text streams line by line |\n| 16.3-16.8 | lockup | Camera pulls back to the whole window on the grey field | Zoom-out ~1.9x to ~0.8x over ~0.4s with motion blur, ease-out landing (expo.out-like) |\n| 16.8-17.13 | lockup | Full window on grey, static | Hold ~0.3s, ends without logo or text |\n\n## Pacing\nMeasured: 3 shots, hard cuts at 1.67 and 11.3; avg 5.71s, median 5.83s. In practice it plays as one continuous camera over a single recording. It moves through ~5 snappy re-frames (zooms and pans of ~0.3-0.4s each) separated by holds of 1-4s while the cursor works. It is fast at the start (zoom in after 0.33s) and fast at the end (pull-out in the last ~0.8s). The middle is real-time interaction. No text cards. Cuts on beat: n/a (no audio).\n\n## Typography\nNone added. All text is product UI (Notion's sans, ~1.5-2.5% of frame height when zoomed, ~5% for the page title). No captions, no headline cards, no lockup wordmark.\n\n## Color and texture\n- Outer field: light warm grey #E7E5E0 with a soft dark halo around the window (shadow ~0 30px 80px rgba(0,0,0,.25)), seen only at the start and end.\n- UI: white #FFFFFF, Notion blue #2383E2 for the Save button and the \"New\" button, pastel status chips (yellow #F7E7B4, purple #E8DEEE).\n- Modal backdrop dims the page to mid-grey (~rgba(0,0,0,.45)).\n- No grain or color grade.\n- Motion blur is the only stylisation: a strong directional blur during camera moves.\n\n## Product UI treatment\nA real screen recording of the actual product at full fidelity, with the real macOS cursor. It is framed as a floating window only in the first and last frames. Everything else is a tight crop (~2x) that re-frames to follow the cursor's area of interest. Typing happens at real speed. Menus, mention picker and streaming AI reply are all real. The camera never rotates or tilts, and moves only in 2D pan/zoom.\n\n## Motion vocabulary\n- Open zoom: whole window to ~2x crop, ~0.3s, power3.inOut, strong motion blur.\n- Follow re-frames: 2D pan/zoom to the next area of interest, ~0.3-0.4s, power2.inOut, with motion blur. Then a hard stop and hold.\n- UI-native animations: menus pop (~0.1s), hover highlights, typing, text streaming.\n- Closing pull-back: ~2x to whole window, ~0.4s, expo.out-like (big first steps, then a settle), motion blur.\n- Two hard cuts trim dead time in the recording.\n- No ambient motion during holds.\n\n## Sound (measured only)\nNo audio track (audio: false). No tempo. Visuals imply no hits.\n\n## Signature techniques\n1. **Recording on a floating window**: place the screen video inside a rounded window (radius ~1% width) at ~78% width, centred on #E7E5E0 with a big soft shadow. Open on this frame for ~0.3s only.\n2. **Motion-blurred snap zoom**: animate a camera wrapper `{scale:2, x:..., y:...}` over 0.3s with power3.inOut. Fake the motion blur by adding `filter: blur(6px)` peaking mid-tween (blur 0 > 6px > 0 on the same timeline), or by compositing 3-4 offset copies at low opacity.\n3. **Cursor-follow re-frame**: keep a list of focus rects keyed to timestamps. At each one, tween the camera to centre that rect at ~2x in 0.35s (power2.inOut), then hold still while the UI action plays.\n4. **Pull-back ending**: in the last ~0.8s, tween the camera from the crop back to the full window (0.4s, expo.out) and hold 0.3s. No logo.\n\n## Rules to copy\n- Show, don't tell: no headline text, captions or logos. Let the real UI carry it.\n- Use one continuous recording and trim dead time with a couple of invisible hard cuts.\n- Open wide for a split second, then snap in to ~2x.\n- Every camera move is short (~0.3-0.4s), motion-blurred and followed by a still hold.\n- Frame the area the cursor is acting on, never the whole screen, during the demo.\n- End by pulling back out to the floating window on a neutral grey field."
