  "description": "Figma: design system hub sneak peek, Guidelines and Code Sources (2026-10-15, 23.72s, 1920x1080). Black kinetic-label cards, card stacks and textured backdrops, ending in a red type-specimen glitch.",
  "body": "# Figma: design system hub sneak peek, Guidelines and Code Sources (2026-10-15, 23.72s, 1920x1080)\nType: feature launch\nLink: https://x.com/figma/status/2110604452214509864\n\n## One-line style\nBlack kinetic-label cards, card stacks and textured backdrops, ending in a red type-specimen glitch.\n\n## Structure\n| Time | Beat | On screen | Motion |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0-1.6 | hook | Black: \"Connect all your libraries / to one system\", centered | Line 1 cuts on yellow, ~0.33s later line 2 appears and all settle white; hold ~1.2s |\n| 1.6-6.6 | demo | Left label + card row: \"Design Libraries\" (component card), \"Code Libraries\" (purple code card), \"Open-source Repos\" (yellow icon card), \"Guidelines\" (dark \"Context files\" card) | Each step: first word cuts on yellow, second word follows ~0.25s later, then white; a new card width-wipes in at the left of the row (~0.4s power3.out) pushing earlier cards right and off frame; ~1.0-1.3s per step |\n| 6.6-9.6 | proof | Light dotted canvas with library/code nodes and connector lines, then \"Design system: Pickup Design 4.0\" node with lines fanning down | Slow zoom-out ~1s, then push-in ~0.7s power2.inOut to the node |\n| 9.6-11.0 | reveal | Web app overview page \"Pickup Design 4.0\" (search bar, system map, issue counts) floating on a grainy green grass-like texture | Hard cut; page scales in slightly ~0.4s and settles |\n| 11.0-12.6 | transition | Black: \"Keep everyone in sync\", one line, centered | Yellow then white ~0.2s later; hold ~1.3s |\n| 12.6-15.9 | demo | Macro: AI chat panel (\"Describe your idea\") on slate blue; cursor clicks book icon; popover \"Design systems / Libraries\" with a toggle switched on | Hard cut to tight crop; popover pops ~0.2s back.out; toggle flips ~0.2s |\n| 15.9-18.2 | demo | Row of blank grey gradient panels becomes purple-outline wireframes, then filled marketplace UI screens | Camera pans left continuously ~2.3s (none/linear); each panel resolves blank to wireframe to full UI in ~0.8s; new blank panels enter from the right |\n| 18.2-20.6 | peak | Black: red/white \"Aa\" type specimens, pill buttons with arrows in a dashed cyan/lilac selection box, row of color dots with hex labels (#FF01E5, #FF7237, #67EF7F) | Pieces build up per frame: dots multiply, buttons stack, \"Aa\" sizes cascade; hex labels scramble (rapid measured cuts 18.17-18.88s) |\n| 20.6-21.4 | lockup | Elements shrink and converge to center | Buttons revert to dots, dots gather into a cluster, \"Aa\" shrinks; ~0.8s power2.in |\n| 21.4-23.72 | lockup | Figma logo, centered, ~22% frame height, on black | Static hold ~2.3s |\n\n## Pacing\n21 hard cuts, 22 shots, average ~1.08s, median ~0.09s (skewed by the frame-by-frame build at 18.17-18.88s). Excluding that cluster, shots run ~1.3-3s. Mostly cut-based; the label sequence (1.6-6.6s) is one continuous shot with stepped text changes every ~1s. Speeds up at the type-specimen build, slows on the final logo hold. 5/21 cuts within 80 ms of the ~126 BPM grid.\n\n## Typography\nNeutral grotesque sans, regular weight, tight tracking, sentence case (\"Keep everyone in sync\"). Headlines ~10% frame height, centered, 1-2 lines. Labels ~9% height, left-aligned at ~1-3% margin, 2 lines of one word each (\"Design / Libraries\"). Text cuts on per word or line, newest piece yellow ~#EEF266 then white. No fades, slides or scale on type. Ending uses a red-on-white \"Aa\" display specimen in a grotesque, stacked in descending sizes (~16%, ~12%, ~5% frame height), and mono hex labels on colored highlight blocks.\n\n## Color and texture\nBlack #000 for title and label cards (no code texture in this cut). Cards: plum ~#5E2050, pale yellow ~#F1FAB0, pale blue-grey ~#D3E1E6, dark grey ~#3A3A3A, dashed lilac component outlines ~#A07CF0. Canvas ~#EFEFEF with dot grid. Grainy green grass-like texture ~#2F9E48 behind the web app. Slate blue ~#8FB0C6 for the AI demo. Ending palette from on-screen labels: magenta #FF01E5, orange #FF7237, red #FF3737, green #67EF7F, cyan #00B6FF, plus red ~#E8253A type blocks and white. Flat; soft shadows only on floating UI.\n\n## Product UI treatment\nReal Figma UI, simplified marketing content. Component, code and file cards cropped to tall 3:4 tiles and treated as graphic blocks. Node graph shown on dotted canvas. AI panel shown macro (2-3x) with a large black arrow cursor (~8% frame height, white outline). Generation shown as grey placeholder to wireframe to filled UI under a continuous pan.\n\n## Motion vocabulary\n- Word cut-on with yellow-to-white settle, ~0.2-0.3s per step.\n- Card insert at the left of a row with width wipe, ~0.4s power3.out; row pushes right and off frame.\n- Zoom-out ~1s expo.out, push-in ~0.7s power2.inOut on canvas.\n- Popover pop ~0.2s back.out(1.7); toggle flip ~0.2s power2.out.\n- Placeholder resolve: grey gradient sheen to outlined wireframe to final UI, ~0.8s, staggered ~0.3s across panels, under a linear pan.\n- Frame-by-frame build of graphic primitives (dots, pills, type blocks), then converge to logo ~0.8s power2.in.\n\n## Sound (measured only)\nAudio present. Tempo estimate ~126.3 BPM. 5 of 21 cuts within 80 ms of the beat grid. The frame-by-frame build at ~18.2-18.9s implies rapid hits, unclear without audio.\n\n## Signature techniques\n1. Label + growing card row: black bg, label at left (2 words, 2 lines, ~9% height); a row of 3:4 cards at ~25% x; each step `gsap.fromTo(newCard, {width:0}, {width:cardW, duration:0.4, ease:\"power3.out\"})` inserted first in a flex row so older cards slide right.\n2. Yellow-settle word reveal: `gsap.set` word 1 visible yellow; +0.25s word 2 visible yellow, word 1 white; +0.25s all white.\n3. Placeholder-to-UI generation: three panels with a grey linear-gradient sheen; at t+0.3s crossfade to an outline-only wireframe layer (lilac 1px boxes); at t+0.6s crossfade to the real UI; stagger panels ~0.3s while the container translates left at constant speed.\n4. Type-specimen burst: on black, place stacked red \"Aa\" blocks, a dashed selection box of arrow pills and a row of color dots with mono hex labels; step new elements in every frame for ~0.7s, scramble hex text, then tween everything to center with scale 0.2 over 0.8s power2.in and cut to the logo.\n5. Textured backdrop for full-page UI: grainy painted texture (green or pink) full-bleed behind a floating app window with soft shadow.\n\n## Rules to copy\n- Put every headline on plain black, centered, sentence case, ~10% height.\n- Flash new words yellow, then settle to white; never fade type.\n- Explain a system by stacking cards one at a time beside a changing label.\n- Crop UI tight and use a large outlined cursor for interaction beats.\n- Show generation as placeholder, then wireframe, then final UI.\n- Build the finale from colorful primitives frame by frame, then collapse to the logo.\n- Hold the logo alone on black for ~2.3s."
