  "description": "Linear: Linear Agent (2026-03-25, 54.91s, 2160x1080). Near-black tilted 3D product UI, shallow focus, slow drifts, typed prompts, whisper-quiet lockup.",
  "body": "# Linear: Linear Agent (2026-03-25, 54.91s, 2160x1080)\nType: product launch\nLink: https://x.com/linear/status/2036825558084878467\n\n## One-line style\nNear-black tilted 3D product UI, shallow focus, slow drifts, typed prompts, whisper-quiet lockup.\n\n## Structure\n| Time | Beat | On screen | Motion |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0.0-3.1 | hook | Full app window (sidebar, empty \"Project spec\" doc) laid on a plane tilted away toward upper right, edges falling into black and blur | Slow dolly-in / drift down-left, ~linear; title sharpens as focus plane settles |\n| 3.1-5.3 | transition | Hard cut (undetected, dark) to extreme close-up of window's bottom-right corner; an \"Ask Linear\" pill fades in | Slow drift; pill fades in ~0.4s |\n| 5.3-10.5 | demo | Composer expands above pill (\"Ask Linear...\" placeholder), then prompt is typed char by char | Panel grows up ~0.6s, power2.out; typing ~10-12 chars/s with bar caret |\n| 10.5-11.25 | transition | Text clears, empty composer holds | Input clears in 1 frame; ~0.6s hold |\n| 11.25-17.0 | reveal | Hard cut to chat panel header + user bubble; answer line fades in, then issue list (IDs, colored status icons, avatars) resolves from scrambled noise glyphs top-down | Each row decodes ~0.5s, stagger ~0.25s; camera keeps creeping |\n| 17.0-21.0 | demo | Re-framed lower on panel; second prompt typed into composer | Typing ~10 chars/s; submit moves text into right-aligned bubble |\n| 21.97-29.7 | reveal | Hard cut to doc canvas: \"Project spec\" title dissolves, new title types on; overview paragraph and table resolve from blur | Title out ~0.5s fade; new title types with soft-blurred leading edge ~0.8s; body blur-to-sharp ~1s, rows stagger ~0.3s |\n| 29.7-35.3 | demo | Cut to sequence/architecture diagram: grey tilted boxes, thin lines, mono labels appear step by step | Lines draw in ~0.4s each; labels fade grey-to-white in sequence ~0.3s apart |\n| 35.3-40.7 | proof | Hard cut to widest shot: whole app (sidebar, doc, docked chat panel) small in frame, still tilted | Slow vertical scroll of doc content (~linear) while panel stays docked |\n| 40.7-45.0 | peak | Hard cut to big close-up of chat thread: reply text and doc reference card appear, then a follow-up line | Lines fade/slide in ~0.4s; very slow drift |\n| 45.0-47.2 | lockup | Black; centered \"Linear\" wordmark blurs into focus, a lavender highlight sweeps letters left to right | Blur ~16px to 0 over ~0.5s, power2.out; sweep ~1s, none |\n| 47.2-50.4 | lockup | Tagline \"At your command.\" reveals after wordmark | Left-to-right wipe with blurred leading edge ~0.7s, lavender tint on newest letters |\n| 50.4-54.9 | lockup | Hard cut to logo mark alone, centered | Static hold ~4.5s |\n\n## Pacing\nmeasure.json reports 0 hard cuts (1 shot) because the frames are so dark; visually there are ~9 hard cuts between camera setups (~3.1, ~11.25, ~22.0, ~29.7, ~35.3, ~40.7, ~45.0, ~50.4 s). Average setup ~6s. Each setup is a continuous slow camera drift, not static. Holds are long: typing plays in real time, chat answers get 4-6s. Pace is even and unhurried throughout; it only \"speeds up\" via faster typing bursts. The final ~10s is lockup and logo hold. Cuts on beat: n/a (0/0 measured).\n\n## Typography\nUI text only until the end: neutral grotesk sans (Inter-like), regular/medium, sentence case. In close-ups UI text is ~3-4.5% of frame height; in wide shots ~1%. Mono font for diagram labels and issue IDs. Lockup: same sans, ~4.5% of frame height, centered, \"Linear.\" in white medium weight, \"At your command.\" regular in slightly lighter grey; tracking normal. 1 word, then 4 words. Enters by blur-to-sharp and left-to-right soft wipe; exits by hard cut. Holds ~3s.\n\n## Color and texture\nPure black surround #000000 with heavy vignette; UI surfaces #15171a to #1e2124, raised panels #24282c with 1px borders ~#2e3236. Text #e8e8e8 primary, #6b7076 muted, placeholders ~#4a4e53. Status icon accents only: yellow ~#e2b31c, green ~#3fae5c, orange-red ~#e0623a. Lockup highlight lavender ~#b3b0ff with soft glow. Strong depth of field: only a band of the tilted plane is sharp, near and far edges blur. No grain visible. Soft dark drop shadows under panels.\n\n## Product UI treatment\nReal high-fidelity product UI (sidebar, breadcrumbs, issue list with avatars, doc with table, diagram). Always on a 3D plane: rotated ~-12 to -20 deg in Z and ~40-55 deg in X so it recedes to upper right. Camera frames cropped details (a corner, a composer, a list) at large scale, with one wide shot. No cursor; interaction is shown by typing with a caret and by content appearing. Content reveals via noise-glyph decode and blur-to-sharp.\n\n## Motion vocabulary\n- Camera drift: continuous slow translate/rotate across each setup, ~2-6% of frame per second, ease none or sine.inOut.\n- Hard cuts between setups, no transitions.\n- Typing: ~10-12 chars/s, constant, caret visible.\n- Panel expand: height grows ~0.6s power2.out.\n- Decode reveal: text rows start as scrambled pixel glyphs and resolve ~0.5s per row, stagger ~0.25s, top to bottom.\n- Blur reveal: filter blur ~10px to 0 + opacity 0.3 to 1 over ~0.8-1s, power2.out, row stagger ~0.3s.\n- Diagram draw: lines scale from 0 ~0.4s power2.out; labels grey-to-white sequentially.\n- Lockup: blur-in, then color sweep across letters, then left-to-right soft wipe for tagline.\n\n## Sound (measured only)\nAudio present. Tempo estimate ~104 BPM. No measured cuts, so no on-beat data. No flashes or visual hits that imply accents; visuals suggest a calm bed.\n\n## Signature techniques\n1. Tilted UI plane with shallow DOF: build UI as a large DOM panel, wrap in a parent with `perspective: 1800px`, apply `rotateX(48deg) rotateZ(-16deg)`; add two blurred copies masked to near and far edges (or a CSS mask gradient with backdrop blur) so only a diagonal band is sharp; radial vignette to #000.\n2. Drift camera: per setup, GSAP tween the plane's x/y/z by ~5-10% of frame over the whole shot, ease none; hard-cut to a new plane transform for the next setup.\n3. Noise decode rows: for each list row, render text as random glyphs (or a pixel-noise canvas) and swap characters to final over ~0.5s; stagger rows 0.25s; fade icons in at the end.\n4. Blur-then-sweep wordmark: centered white word, tween `filter: blur(16px)->0`, opacity 0->1, 0.5s power2.out; then animate a lavender background-clip gradient across the text (background-position -100% -> 200%, ~1s, none) with a matching text-shadow glow.\n5. Soft wipe tagline: mask-image linear-gradient with a ~15% feather, move from left to right over ~0.7s power1.inOut; newest letters tinted lavender then settle to grey.\n\n## Rules to copy\n- Keep everything near-black; let only UI text and tiny status colors carry light.\n- Never show UI flat; always on a tilted plane with focus falloff.\n- Keep the camera always drifting slowly; change angle with hard cuts, not transitions.\n- Show interaction by typing in real time, not by cursors.\n- Reveal generated content through decode or blur-to-sharp, row by row.\n- Hold each beat long enough to read (4-8s).\n- End on plain centered type, then the logo mark alone on black."
