  "description": "Linear: Loop triggers from Slack and GitHub (2026-10-22, 29.72s, 1920x1080). Flat dark chat UI typed in real time, soft fades, plain centered captions.",
  "body": "# Linear: Loop triggers from Slack and GitHub (2026-10-22, 29.72s, 1920x1080)\nType: feature launch\nLink: https://x.com/linear/status/2113319962156867752\n\n## One-line style\nFlat dark chat UI typed in real time, soft fades, plain centered captions.\n\n## Structure\n| Time | Beat | On screen | Motion |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0.0-7.8 | hook / demo | A single chat composer, flat and wide (~85% frame width) on near-black; a mention chip then a multi-line instruction with bullets is typed | Typing ~12-14 chars/s, caret visible; composer grows one line per new bullet (~0.2s); no camera move |\n| 7.8-8.1 | transition | Composer vanishes, the same text reappears as a posted message with avatar, name, timestamp | Composer fades ~0.1s; message lines fade in top-down, stagger ~0.05s, total ~0.25s |\n| 8.1-10.0 | demo | Posted message holds | Static |\n| 10.0-12.3 | reveal | App reply appears below (\"Loop created...\") | Fades from ~30% to 100% opacity ~0.3s, power2.out |\n| 12.3-19.4 | proof | Three follow-up bot messages, each with an issue card (title, ID, Status / Assignee with lavender mention chips) | Thread scrolls up ~0.4s power2.out as each new message arrives; new message fades in with slight blur ~0.4s; ~2.5s between messages |\n| 19.4-20.3 | transition | Whole thread blurs and fades to background | Blur 0 to ~12px + opacity to 0 over ~0.7s, power1.in |\n| 20.3-22.4 | peak | Centered caption \"GitHub loop triggers\" | Fade + slight blur-in ~0.4s; hold ~1.6s |\n| 22.4-23.4 | transition | Caption fades out, gap | Fade out ~0.5s, ~0.3s empty |\n| 23.4-25.0 | peak | Centered caption \"Now available\" | Blur-in fade ~0.3s; hold ~1.2s; fade out ~0.5s |\n| 25.4-29.4 | lockup | Logo mark + \"Linear\" wordmark centered | Fade in ~0.25s; static hold ~4s; cut to pure black last ~0.3s |\n\n## Pacing\n0 hard cuts measured (1 shot); visually also no cuts. It is one continuous flat frame with in-place fades, a scroll, and a blur dissolve to captions. Typing dominates the first ~8s; bot messages land every ~2.5s; captions hold ~1.5s each; logo holds ~4s. Speeds up slightly in the message stack (12-19s), slows for the captions. Tempo estimate 160 BPM; no cut data to compare to beat.\n\n## Typography\nUI: neutral grotesk sans (Inter-like), regular, sentence case, ~3-3.5% of frame height, left-aligned as in the real app. Captions: same sans, regular/medium, ~6% of frame height, centered, sentence/title case (\"GitHub loop triggers\", \"Now available\"), 2-3 words, white. Enter by fade with slight blur-in ~0.3-0.4s, exit by fade ~0.5s. Lockup wordmark ~7% of height beside a round mark of similar height.\n\n## Color and texture\nFlat near-black background ~#0b0c0e (ends on #000000). Composer/card surfaces ~#15171a with 1px borders ~#26292d. Text #e3e4e6 primary, #8a8d92 secondary, timestamps ~#5d6066. Accent only on mention chips (bg ~#2f2f5a, text ~#9fa1ff) and the send button ~#5b5bd6. No gradients, no grain, no glow, no shadows.\n\n## Product UI treatment\nSimplified but faithful recreation of a chat app (composer toolbar icons, avatars, bot \"APP\" badge, link-unfurl issue cards). Shown flat, front-on, cropped to the content column; no window chrome, no device. No cursor; interaction shown by typing with a caret. Camera never zooms or pans; only the thread scrolls.\n\n## Motion vocabulary\n- Typing: constant ~13 chars/s, caret bar, new bullet lines push the composer taller ~0.2s power2.out.\n- Send: composer out ~0.1s, posted message in ~0.25s with tiny line stagger.\n- New message: thread scrolls up by the new message height ~0.4s power2.out; new block opacity 0.3 to 1 plus blur ~4px to 0 over ~0.4s.\n- Scene exit: full-frame blur + fade ~0.7s.\n- Caption in/out: opacity 0 to 1 with blur ~6px to 0, ~0.35s power2.out; out by opacity ~0.5s power1.in; ~0.3s empty gap between captions.\n- No overshoot anywhere.\n\n## Sound (measured only)\nAudio present. Tempo estimate ~160 BPM. No hard cuts, so no on-beat data. No flashes or visual hits implied.\n\n## Signature techniques\n1. Real-time composer: a DOM textarea look-alike; GSAP steps a character index at ~13 chars/s (ease none) with a blinking caret; mention token rendered as a lavender chip as soon as it is completed.\n2. Send-to-message swap: at send, fade composer to 0 in 0.1s, then mount the message block (avatar, name, time, body) with children opacity 0 to 1, y 4px to 0, stagger 0.05s.\n3. Scrolling thread: keep messages in a column; on each new message, tween column y by minus its height over 0.4s power2.out while the new block fades in from 0.3 opacity with blur 4px to 0.\n4. Blur dissolve to caption: tween the whole UI layer `filter: blur(12px)` and opacity to 0 over 0.7s; then fade a centered caption in with blur 6px to 0 over 0.35s.\n5. Quiet lockup: centered mark + wordmark, fade in 0.25s, hold ~4s, cut to black.\n\n## Rules to copy\n- Show the feature by typing it, at readable real-time speed.\n- Keep the UI flat, front-on and large; no window chrome, no camera moves.\n- Use color only for mention chips and one send button; everything else greyscale.\n- Advance the story by scrolling a thread, not by cutting.\n- Exit UI with a full-frame blur fade before any caption.\n- Captions are 2-3 words, centered, ~6% of frame height, alone on black.\n- Leave short empty gaps between captions; end on a plain mark + wordmark."
