  "description": "Motion: Muse for motion design (2026-09-20, 30.05s, 1920x1080). Clean white title stack, then a phone chat demo on a sky-blue gradient, close-cropped and drifting.",
  "body": "# Motion: Muse for motion design (2026-09-20, 30.05s, 1920x1080)\nType: product launch\nLink: https://x.com/motion_so/status/2101743483123892677\n\n## One-line style\nClean white title stack, then a phone chat demo on a sky-blue gradient, close-cropped and drifting.\n\n## Structure\n| Time | Beat | On screen | Motion |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0-0.03 | (stray frame) | One frame of the phone scene | Hard cut (measured 0.03) |\n| 0.03-1.0 | hook | White. Blue scribble \"m\" logo mark, top-centre, ~7% height | Logo fades in over ~0.1s, then holds |\n| 1.0-1.67 | reveal | Bold \"Muse\" appears under the logo, ~8% height | Fades in with a ~1.5% upward rise, ~0.3s, power2.out |\n| 1.67-3.0 | reveal | Regular \"for motion design\" beneath, ~3.5% height | Same fade + small rise, ~0.3s |\n| 3.0-4.03 | reveal | Tiny \"Powered by Motion\" with a 4-dot icon near the bottom, ~1.2% height | Fades in; whole stack holds |\n| 4.03-6.23 | demo | Sky-blue diagonal gradient; black-bezel phone with a chat app (~80% height), cursor drifts in from the right toward the input | Hard cut; phone near-static with a very slow drift |\n| 6.23-8.0 | demo | Hard cut to a ~2.5x crop of the phone's bottom: input field + tab bar; \"Create a motion design video.\" types in; cursor clicks send | Typing ~2 chars/frame; slow camera drift |\n| 8.0-13.0 | demo | Prompt becomes a blue user bubble; a grey status card \"Motion / Creating scenes...\" with a thin blue progress bar; label changes to \"Adding sound...\", then \"Rendering your video...\" | Camera slowly pushes and pans (~10% over 5s, sine.inOut); progress bar fills left to right |\n| 13.0-15.3 | proof | Chat scrolls to a \"Your motion design / v1 Preview\" card with a green plant illustration playing | Content scrolls up ~0.5s (power2.inOut); preview animates inside the card |\n| 15.3-19.0 | proof | Generated video full-frame: light green bg, white card, handwritten green all-caps \"POCKET GARDEN / LAUNCHES / TODAY\" writing itself on | Cut/fast zoom into the preview (unclear which); letters write on ~0.1s each |\n| 19.0-21.3 | demo | Back to the cropped phone input: \"Change that.\" typed and sent; \"Updating with Motion...\" | Hard cut back; typing; slow drift |\n| 21.3-27.03 | proof | Preview card updates from \"v1 Preview\" to \"v2 Updated\": many floating chat bubbles with avatars, then an ending card \"Pocket Garden\" in green italic serif | Card scrolls in; badge swaps; slow push |\n| 27.03-29.67 | lockup | White end card: left-aligned \"Muse for motion design\" (~4.5% height), tiny grey \"available\", large \"motion.so\" (~8% height); blue logo mark at right (~9% height) | Hard cut. Title and logo appear first; \"available\" fades in at ~27.6s; \"motion.so\" fades/rises in at ~28.0s (~0.25s, power2.out); hold ~1.7s |\n| 29.67-30.05 | lockup | Black | Hard cut |\n\n## Pacing\nMeasured: 4 hard cuts (0.03, 4.03, 6.23, 27.03), 5 shots, avg 6.01s, median 3.02s. The long middle shot (6.23-27.03, ~21s) is one continuous, slowly drifting camera on the phone UI. Within it, the cut-backs to the input and the full-frame preview are probably hidden cuts or fast zooms that detection missed. Title beats arrive ~0.67-1.3s apart. Demo holds run 2-5s. The pace is relaxed and even throughout, with a slow, calm ending. Cuts on beat: 1/4 at ~82.8 BPM.\n\n## Typography\n- Neutral grotesk sans (Inter-like) throughout.\n- Title: \"Muse\" bold ~700 at ~8% height. Subtitle \"for motion design\" regular ~400 at ~3.5%. Credit \"Powered by Motion\" ~1.2%. All centred in a vertical stack under the logo.\n- End card: left-aligned at ~13% from the left. \"Muse for motion design\" medium ~500 at ~4.5%. \"available\" ~1.4% in grey #9A9A9A. \"motion.so\" regular at ~8%, slightly tight tracking. Logo on the right at ~80% width.\n- Sentence/lower case, no punctuation.\n- 1-4 words per line.\n- Entry: fade + small upward rise (~1.5% height, ~0.3s, power2.out), one line at a time, ~0.6-1.3s apart. No exits (hard cut).\n- In-UI type is ~4% height when cropped.\n- The generated video uses a handwritten all-caps green font and a green italic serif. These belong to the demo content, not the brand frame.\n\n## Color and texture\n- Title and end cards: pure white #FFFFFF, text #111111, logo blue #1F6FE0.\n- Demo bg: diagonal linear gradient from near-white #F3F8FD (top-left) to sky blue #7DB9EE (right), with soft, even light.\n- Phone: black bezel #111, white screen.\n- UI accents: user bubble pale blue #CFE3F7, status card grey #EDEDEF, progress bar blue #2C7BE5.\n- Demo content: mint #E6F7E2, leaf green #2E8B3A.\n- No grain or glow. The phone has a thin, subtle shadow.\n\n## Product UI treatment\nA real (or faithfully rebuilt) phone chat UI inside a simple black-bezel device frame. It is shown wide once, then mostly as a tight ~2.5x crop of the lower half (input + tab bar) or of the conversation area. A real-looking cursor clicks send. Typing is live. The camera handles UI with slow continuous drift/push and gentle scrolls rather than snappy zooms. The output (the generated video) is shown both as a thumbnail in a card and full-frame.\n\n## Motion vocabulary\n- Logo-mark appear: opacity 0 to 1, ~0.1s.\n- Title lines: opacity 0 to 1 + y +1.5% to 0, ~0.3s, power2.out, ~0.67-1.3s between lines.\n- Camera drift on device: continuous scale/translate of ~5-10% over 3-5s, sine.inOut or none.\n- Chat scroll: content translateY ~0.5s, power2.inOut.\n- Status card: label text swaps every ~1.5-2s; thin progress bar width grows, ease none.\n- Version badge swap: \"v1 Preview\" to \"v2 Updated\", instant.\n- End card build: elements appear one by one (title+logo, then caption, then URL), ~0.4-0.5s apart, fade + small rise.\n- Transitions: hard cuts between the title, phone wide, phone crop and end card. No wipes.\n\n## Sound (measured only)\nAudio present. Tempo estimate ~82.8 BPM. Cuts on beat: 1/4. No flashes or shakes that would imply hits. Unclear beyond that.\n\n## Signature techniques\n1. **Stacked title reveal**: on white, a centred column of logo mark (7vh), bold name (8vh), regular tagline (3.5vh) and tiny \"powered by\" credit (1.2vh). Reveal each with `from({opacity:0,y:\"1.5vh\",duration:0.3,ease:\"power2.out\"})`, spaced ~0.7-1.3s apart.\n2. **Gradient stage + device crop**: a full-bleed `linear-gradient(115deg,#F3F8FD 0%,#7DB9EE 100%)` with a phone frame (black 1.2vh border, radius 6vh). Show it wide for ~2s, then hard cut to a 2.5x crop of the input area and type the prompt.\n3. **Agent progress card**: a grey rounded card with a small brand label, a status line that swaps text every ~1.7s (\"Creating scenes...\", \"Adding sound...\", \"Rendering...\"), and a 2px blue bar filling left to right linearly over the whole sequence. Under it, keep a very slow camera push.\n4. **Result-in-card then full-frame**: scroll the chat to reveal a result card with the output playing inside. Then cut to the output full-frame for ~3s, and cut back to the chat to iterate (\"Change that.\") with a v1-to-v2 badge swap.\n5. **Left-aligned URL end card**: on white, a small title line, tiny grey caption, big URL, with the logo mark far right on the same baseline band. Build it in 3 steps ~0.5s apart, hold ~1.7s, then cut to black.\n\n## Rules to copy\n- Open and close on pure white with the logo mark. Put the demo on a soft blue gradient in between.\n- Reveal text one line at a time with a gentle fade-up. Never animate words individually.\n- Keep the device frame plain, and crop tightly into the area where the action happens.\n- Keep the camera alive with slow drift and push during the demo. Avoid snappy zooms.\n- Show the AI working with a status card and thin progress bar, then show the actual output.\n- Show iteration: prompt, result, short revision prompt, updated result.\n- End on a left-aligned URL card with the logo on the right and a short hold."
